From: Codex <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] musb: keep RTL8723BU HCI bulk off endpoint 5

The F1C100S MUSB controller has five non-control hardware endpoints. With
RTL8723BU Wi-Fi active, the generic allocator places Bluetooth HCI bulk IN
(USB endpoint 2) on hardware endpoint 5. HCI commands then receive no events.
Conversely, when Bluetooth reserves the lower endpoints first, Wi-Fi receives
no packets after being placed on endpoint 5.

Use the controller's multiplexed bulk-IN queue for the Bluetooth HCI bulk
endpoint, preserving the working endpoint allocation for Wi-Fi and keeping
HCI bulk traffic off endpoint 5.

--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
@@ -2065,6 +2065,20 @@ static int musb_schedule(
 		hw_ep = musb->control_ep;
 		goto success;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * RTL8723BU exposes Bluetooth HCI bulk IN as USB endpoint 2. When
+	 * Wi-Fi owns the first free RX endpoint, the generic allocator puts
+	 * this transfer on F1C100S MUSB endpoint 5, where HCI events stall.
+	 * Use the controller's multiplexed bulk RX queue instead and leave
+	 * endpoint 5 unused by the HCI path.
+	 */
+	if (is_in && musb_qh_is_rtl8723bu(qh) && qh->epnum == 2 &&
+	    qh->type == USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_BULK && musb->bulk_ep) {
+		hw_ep = musb->bulk_ep;
+		head = &musb->in_bulk;
+		if (qh->dev)
+			qh->intv_reg =
+				(USB_SPEED_HIGH == qh->dev->speed) ? 8 : 4;
+		goto success;
+	}
 
 	if (is_in && musb_qh_is_aic(qh) && qh->type == USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_BULK &&
 	    musb->bulk_ep) {
